On 2009-02-10, brigade@monger.net <brigade@monger.net> wrote:
> I've got to the plane of fire, and I'm trying to find the portal, but
> I keep getting slowed down by "Monsters Appear Out Of Nowhere!"
>
> Luckily, I had 2 amulets of life saving, but they're both used up
> after I get surrounded and mowed down by the hoard, and it still keeps
> happening.  What's causing this?
>
> Thanks!

Two reasons.  You killed the Wizard, and one of his post-mortem special
effects is to cast "Summon Nasties" centered on you.  Second, there's a
high-level caster (a master or arch-lich, a nalfenshee, an archon...)
spamcasting "Summon Nasties" out of your sight.  Either one of those would do
that by itself, although if it's really frequent, it's usually more the second
than the first.  You need to be fast, or very fast, be unburdened, and make
use of the terrain better.  If there's a caster, you need to kill it.  When
you get surrounded, if you 'a'pply a wand of teleportation with at least one
charge, it will break, and teleport the monsters surrounding you; that will at
least give you some breathing room.

Also, if you're getting 'mowed down' quickly, you may have an insufficently low
armor class, or you may just be burdened or worse, or both.  If you're not
over lava, you can always engrave Elbereth, as well, to give you time to sort
things out.

